※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ An arm that writes memory and then leaves the function: what it wrote is on a way that
※ never reaches the code after the `if`, so that code reads memory as it was before the arm.
※ The token the arm left behind is not one anything after the join can see.

@[impure]
fn early(trail: &mut u64, leave: bool) → u8:
    if leave:
        trail⌖ ← 5u64
        return 7u8
    trail⌖ ← trail⌖ + 1u64
    8u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let trail: mut u64 = 0u64
    let one: u8 = early(&mut trail, false)
    if one ≠ 8u8 ∨ trail ≠ 1u64:
        return 2u6
    0u6
